# Git and Bash

Run project commands in Linux. Source `dev/linux/env.sh` or use
`bash dev/linux/run.sh COMMAND`. Keep WSL checkouts on the Linux filesystem.
The sole Windows entrypoint is `dev/equipqr.bat`; it only launches WSL and the browser.

Use quoted arguments and Bash arrays. Never execute dotenv content as shell code.
Use UTF-8 body files with `gh pr create/edit --body-file` and `git commit -F` for
multiline text. Preserve existing PR footer links when editing descriptions.
Use JSON input for review replies, with the parent comment ID in `in_reply_to`.
Inspect failures before retrying a publishing command to avoid duplicate comments.

Follow the PR merge workflow and its verification gates. List worktrees before
removing one; stop its managed stack first. Verify a remote merge independently
if local branch cleanup fails because the branch is checked out in a worktree.
